.TH VEDIT 1 "2026-10-06" "vedit 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vedit \- a single-file visual text editor for primitive terminals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vedit
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vedit
is a full-screen text editor with an MS-EDIT style menu and chrome. It runs on
plain terminals, including slow or limited ones, and draws its frame with
Unicode box-drawing, DEC VT100 line-drawing, or plain ASCII depending on the
client. It has two key personalities: a modeless (MS-EDIT) one by default and a
modal
.I vi
one, toggled at run time with
.BR F2 .
.PP
A missing
.I file
opens as a new, named buffer. Opening a file that is already open, even by a
different spelling such as a symlink or a
.RB \(lq ./ \(rq
detour, switches to the existing buffer instead of loading a second copy. When
run from the command line, vedit requires a terminal on both standard input and
standard output.
.PP
Press
.B F1
inside the editor for the key bindings of the active personality, and open the
Help menu, or press
.B t
on the key-bindings screen, for the built-in tutorials.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-utf8
Draw the frame with Unicode box-drawing characters.
.TP
.B \-\-dec
Draw the frame with DEC VT100 line-drawing characters.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-ascii
Draw the frame with plain ASCII
.RB ( + ", " \- ", " | ).
The default is UTF-8 under a UTF-8 locale, otherwise ASCII. It can also be set
with
.B VEDIT_BOX=utf8|dec|ascii
or
.BR VEDIT_ASCII .
.TP
.B \-\-16color
Map colors to the 16 ANSI colors for old clients.
.TP
.B \-\-256color
Use the full 256-color palette. The default is 256 when
.B TERM
or
.B COLORTERM
says so, otherwise 16. It can also be set with
.BR VEDIT_COLORS=256|16 .
.TP
.B \-\-scroll
Use the VT100 scroll region when scrolling, which is faster on a slow link but
needs a client that supports it.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-scroll
Repaint instead of scrolling. This is the default. The behavior can also be set
with
.BR VEDIT_SCROLL=0|1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Read settings from
.I FILE
instead of the default locations.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Skip the configuration file entirely.
.SH KEYS
This is a brief orientation. Press
.B F1
in the editor for the full, personality-specific list.
.SS Modeless (MS-EDIT)
.TP
.B arrows, Home, End, PgUp, PgDn
Move the cursor; Ctrl+Home and Ctrl+End jump to the start and end of the file.
.TP
.B Shift+arrows
Extend a selection.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-C ", " Ctrl\-X ", " Ctrl\-V
Copy (the current line when nothing is selected), cut, and paste.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-Z ", " Ctrl\-Y
Undo and redo.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-F ", " Ctrl\-R
Incremental find, and replace confirming each match.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-S ", " Ctrl\-Q
Save and quit; both prompt when needed.
.TP
.BR F10 ", Alt+" letter
Open the menu bar.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-W " " m
Open the menu bar from inside a terminal buffer, where the other keys go to
the running program.
.B Ctrl\-W
is the prefix for terminal control:
.B w
and
.B W
switch to the next and previous buffer,
.BR 1 ".." 9
switch to that buffer,
.B n
opens another terminal,
.B r
or
.B R
reposts the output into a new buffer as text or as art,
.B c
or
.B q
closes this one, and
.B Ctrl\-W
again sends a literal Ctrl\-W to the program.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-W " " s ", " b ", " w ", " c
From a text buffer: open a shell in a pane under the text (or focus the one
there), show the current buffer in the pane with another above it, move the
focus into the pane or back, and close the pane. The build commands show
their output in the same pane.
.TP
.BR F1 ", " F2
Show the key bindings, and toggle the vi personality.
.TP
.B Table view
A .csv, .tsv or .tab file opens as a grid (also
.B :table
on any buffer). Arrows, Tab and Shift+Tab move by cell; Enter edits the cell
in the prompt line, typing replaces it, Delete clears it, Ctrl\-C and Ctrl\-V
copy and paste a cell, Ctrl\-F searches from it. The ex commands
.BR :rowadd [ ! ] ", " :rowdel ", " :coladd [ ! ] ", " :coldel ", " :colwidth
and
.B :cell
insert and delete rows and columns, set a column width, and jump to a cell;
in vi style
.BR "h j k l" ", " "a i c s x" ", " "O o dd yy p P"
and
.B u
work on cells and rows.
.TP
.BI : [range] sort [!] " [n] [i] [N]"
Sort the lines of the range (the buffer, or a table's data rows) by the key
starting at column N, as strings or with
.B n
as decimal numbers;
.B i
ignores case and
.B !
reverses. In a table the key is the cursor column's cell. Edit > Sort Lines
asks the same in a dialog.
.SS vi
NORMAL mode has the usual motions
.RB ( "h j k l" ", " "0 ^ $" ", " "w b e" ", " "gg G" ", " "f F t T" )
and counts, operators
.RB ( "d c y" )
with motions, visual modes
.RB ( v " / " V " / Ctrl-V" ),
registers, marks, and a jump list.
.B :
runs ex commands and
.B /
searches. Press
.B F2
to return to the modeless keys.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from a gitconfig-style file. Without
.BR \-\-config ,
vedit uses
.BR $VEDIT_CONFIG ,
then
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vedit/config ,
then
.BR ~/.veditrc .
Keys are dotted and may be grouped under section headers. Booleans accept
.BR on / off ,
.BR yes / no ,
.BR true / false ,
or
.BR 1 / 0 .
The main sections are
.B [ui]
(scheme, line numbers, word wrap, box mode, colors),
.B [edit]
(personality, auto-indent, swap and backup files, format-on-save),
.B [indent]
(tabs versus spaces),
.B [art]
(the art view for .ans files: view on/off, grid width),
.B [table]
(the table view for CSV and TSV: view on/off, header row, column width),
.BR [tags] ,
.BR [cc] ,
.BR [error] ,
.BR [syntax] ,
and per-language
.BI [command\  """lang"""]
sections for the compile, build, run, and format commands. See
.B README.md
for the full list.
.PP
Keys that commonly vary per project can be overridden by an environment
variable named
.B VEDIT_
followed by the key uppercased with each
.RB \(lq . \(rq
turned into
.RB \(lq _ \(rq,
for example
.B VEDIT_TAGS_FILE
or
.BR VEDIT_COMMAND_C_FORMAT .
A set, non-empty value wins over the file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VEDIT_CONFIG
Path to the configuration file.
.TP
.BR VEDIT_BOX ", " VEDIT_ASCII
Override the box-drawing mode.
.TP
.B VEDIT_COLORS
Override the color depth
.RB ( 256 " or " 16 ).
.TP
.B VEDIT_SCROLL
Enable
.RB ( 1 )
or disable
.RB ( 0 )
the scroll-region fast path.
.TP
.BI VEDIT_ "KEY"
Per-key overrides for the project-varying config keys (see CONFIGURATION).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.veditrc
Default configuration file (after
.B $VEDIT_CONFIG
and the XDG path).
.TP
.BI . name .swp
Crash-recovery swap file written beside an edited file, unless relocated with
.BR edit.swapdir .
.TP
.IB name ~
Previous version kept on save when
.B edit.backup
is on, unless relocated with
.BR edit.backupdir .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B vedit
exits 0 on a normal quit and non-zero on a usage error, an unreadable file, or
when input ends unexpectedly. The vi
.B :cq
command exits with a non-zero status on purpose.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation in
.BR README.md .
.SH NOTES
Dirty buffers are snapshotted to swap files while the editor is idle and flushed
again when it is terminated by a signal, so a crash or a kill loses little or no
unsaved work. Reopen the file afterward to recover from the swap.
